-project-team)\n\n\n## Code of Conduct\n\nThis project and everyone participating in it is governed by the\n[KeyPass Code of Conduct](https://github.com/yogeshpaliyal/KeyPass/blob/master/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).\nBy participating, you are expected to uphold this code. Please report unacceptable behaviour\nto <yogeshpaliyal.foss+keypass@gmail.com>.\n\n\n## I Have a Question\n\n> If you want to ask a question, we assume that you have read the available [Documentation]().\n\nBefore you ask a question, it is best to search for existing [Issues](https://github.com/yogeshpaliyal/KeyPass/issues) that might help you. In case you have found a suitable issue and still need clarification, you can write your question in this issue. It is also advisable to search the internet for answers first.\n\nIf you then still feel the need to ask a question and need clarification, we recommend the following:\n\n- Open an [Issue](https://github.com/yogeshpaliyal/KeyPass/issues/new).\n- Provide as much context as you can about what you're running into.\n- Provide project and platform versions (nodejs, npm, etc), depending on what seems relevant.\n\nWe will then take care of the issue as soon as possible.\n\n<!--\nYou might want to create a separate issue tag for questions and include it in this description. People should then tag their issues accordingly.\n\nDepending on how large the project is, you may want to outsource the questioning, e.g. to Stack Overflow or Gitter. You may add additional contact and information possibilities:\n- IRC\n- Slack\n- Gitter\n- Stack Overflow tag\n- Blog\n- FAQ\n- Roadmap\n- E-Mail List\n- Forum\n-->\n\n## I Want To Contribute\n\n> ### Legal Notice <!-- omit in toc -->\n> When contributing to this project, you must agree that you have authored 100% of the content, that you have the necessary rights to the content and that the content you contribute may be provided under the project licence.\n\n### Reporting Bugs\n\n<!-- omit in toc -->\n#### Before Submitting a Bug Report\n\nA good bug report shouldn't leave others needing to chase you up for more information. Therefore, we ask you to investigate carefully, collect information and describe the issue in detail in your report. Please complete the following steps in advance to help us fix any potential bug as fast as possible.\n\n- Make sure that you are using the latest version.\n- Determine if your bug is really a bug and not an error on your side e.g. using incompatible environment components/versions (Make sure that you have read the [documentation](). If you are looking for support, you might want to check [this section](#i-have-a-question)).\n- To see if other users have experienced (and potentially already solved) the same issue you are having, check if there is not already a bug report existing for your bug or error in the [bug tracker](https://github.com/yogeshpaliyal/KeyPass/issues?q=label%3Abug).\n- Also make sure to search the internet (including Stack Overflow) to see if users outside of the GitHub community have discussed the issue.\n- Collect information about the bug:\n  - Stack trace (Traceback)\n  - OS, Platform and Version (Windows, Linux, macOS, x86, ARM)\n  - Version of the interpreter, compiler, SDK, runtime environment, package manager, depending on what seems relevant.\n  - Possibly your input and the output\n  - Can you reliably reproduce the issue? And can you also reproduce it with older versions?\n\n<!-- omit in toc -->\n#### How Do I Submit a Good Bug Report?\n\n> You must never report security related issues, vulnerabilities or bugs including sensitive information to the issue tracker, or elsewhere in public. Instead sensitive bugs must be sent by email to <yogeshpaliyal.foss+keypass@gmail.com>.\n<!-- You may add a PGP key to allow the messages to be sent encrypted as well. -->\n\nWe use GitHub issues to track bugs and errors. If you run into an issue with the project:\n\n- Open an [Issue](https://github.com/yogeshpaliyal/KeyPass/issues/new). (Since we can't be sure at this point whether it is a bug or not, we ask you not to talk about a bug yet and not to label the issue.)\n- Explain the behaviour you would expect and the actual behaviour.\n- Please provide as much context as possible and describe the *reproduction steps* that someone else can follow to recreate the issue on their own. This usually includes your code. For good bug reports you should isolate the problem and create a reduced test case.\n- Provide the information you collected in the previous section.\n\nOnce it's filed:\n\n- The project team will label the issue accordingly.\n- A team member will try to reproduce the issue with your provided steps. If there are no reproduction steps or no obvious way to reproduce the issue, the team will ask you for those steps and mark the issue as `needs-repro`. Bugs with the `needs-repro` tag will not be addressed until they are reproduced.\n- If the team is able to reproduce the issue, it will be marked `needs-fix`, as well as possibly other tags (such as `critical`), and the issue will be left to be [implemented by someone](#your-first-code-contribution).\n\n<!-- You might want to create an issue template for bugs and errors that can be used as a guide and that defines the structure of the information to be included. If you do so, reference it here in the description. -->\n\n\n### Suggesting Enhancements\n\nThis section guides you through submitting an enhancement suggestion for KeyPass, **including completely new features and minor improvements to existing functionality**. Following these guidelines will help maintainers and the community to understand your suggestion and find related suggestions.\n\n<!-- omit in toc -->\n#### Before Submitting an Enhancement\n\n- Make sure that you are using the latest version.\n- Read the [documentation]() carefully and find out if the functionality is already covered, maybe by an individual configuration.\n- Perform a [search](https://github.com/yogeshpaliyal/KeyPass/issues) to see if the enhancement has already been suggested. If it has, add a comment to the existing issue instead of opening a new one.\n- Find out whether your idea fits with the scope and aims of the project. It's up to you to make a strong case to convince the project's developers of the merits of this feature. Keep in mind that we want features that will be useful to the majority of our users and not just a small subset. If you're just targeting a minority of users, consider writing an add-on/plugin library.\n\n<!-- omit in toc -->\n#### How Do I Submit a Good Enhancement Suggestion?\n\nEnhancement suggestions are tracked as [GitHub issues](https://github.com/yogeshpaliyal/KeyPass/issues).\n\n- Use a **clear and descriptive title** for the issue to identify the suggestion.\n- Provide a **step-by-step description of the suggested enhancement** in as many details as possible.\n- **Describe the current behaviour** and **explain which behaviour you expected to see instead** and why. At this point you can also tell which alternatives do not work for you.\n- You may want to **include screenshots and animated GIFs** which help you demonstrate the steps or point out the part which the suggestion is related to. You can use [this tool](https://www.cockos.com/licecap/) to record GIFs on macOS and Windows, and [this tool](https://github.com/colinkeenan/silentcast) or [this tool](https://github.com/GNOME/byzanz) on Linux. <!-- this should only be included if the project has a GUI -->\n- **Explain why this enhancement would be useful** to most KeyPass users. You may also want to point out the other projects that solved it better and which could serve as inspiration.\n\n<!-- You might want to create an issue template for enhancement suggestions that can be used as a guide and that defines the structure of the information to be included. If you do so, reference it here in the description. -->\n\n### Your First Code Contribution\n<!-- TODO\ninclude Setup of env, IDE and typical getting started instructions?\n\n-->\n\n### Improving The Documentation\n<!-- TODO\nUpdating, improving and correcting the documentation\n\n-->\n\n## Styleguides\n### Commit Messages\n<!-- TODO\n\n-->\n\n## Join The Project Team\n<!-- TODO -->\n\n<!-- omit in toc -->\n## Attribution\nThis guide is based on the **contributing-gen**. [Make your own](https://github.com/bttger/contributing-gen)!"}, {'path': 'README.md', 'content': "## 🤝 Contributing\n\nContributions are what make the open-source community such an amazing place to learn, inspire, and create. Any\ncontributions you make are **greatly appreciated**.\n\n1. Open an issue first to discuss what you would like to change.\n1. Fork the Project\n1. Create your feature branch (`git checkout -b feature/amazing-feature`)\n1. Commit your changes (`git commit -m 'Add some amazing feature'`)\n1. Push to the branch (`git push origin feature/amazing-feature`)\n1. Open a pull request\n\nPlease make sure to update tests as appropriate."}], 'branch_policy': {}, 'compatibility_policy': {}, 'migration_assessment': {'usage_kind': 'unknown', 'evidence': ['The key passed to Cipher.init comes from getKey(). It is either an existing AndroidKeyStore SecretKeyEntry with alias "secret" or a key created by createKey() through KeyGenerator.getInstance(ALGORITHM) and generateKey(). No literal or compiled-in key bytes appear in this path.', "The detector's NOT OBSERVED report means the runtime monitor saw no tracked generator for the key object at CryptoManager.kt:42. It is not a positive contradiction. A plausible but unconfirmed explanation is that the key came from KeyStore.getEntry, which the monitor does not track as a producer.", 'Encryption init uses no explicit IV spec. The IV is the one the provider generates, read back with cipher.iv and written to the output stream ahead of the ciphertext. The key spec sets setRandomizedEncryptionRequired(true).'], 'legacy_compatibility_required': True, 'safe_strategy': 'No edit is proposed. If the maintainers later choose an authenticated mode such as AES/GCM/NoPadding, existing CBC-written files must remain readable. That needs a versioned format or a fallback decrypt path, and it is a maintainer decision.', 'policy_authorized': False}, 'publication_considerations': [{'category': 'analyzer_reconfirmation', 'description': 'The pipeline does not rerun the dynamic analyzer, so it cannot show whether the monitor tracks a KeyStore-held key as a generator.', 'kind': 'analyzer_acceptance', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['C3']}, {'category': 'compatibility_contract', 'description': 'Any move away from CBC, for example to GCM, changes the format of the encrypted DataStore file: a length byte, then the IV, then the ciphertext. Existing user settings files must stay readable. No migration path is shown.', 'kind': 'stored_format', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['C5', 'C6']}], 'publication_blocker_record': {'decision': 'MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW', 'blockers': [{'category': 'analyzer_reconfirmation', 'kind': 'analyzer_acceptance', 'description': 'The pipeline does not rerun the dynamic analyzer, so it cannot show whether the monitor tracks a KeyStore-held key as a generator.', 'discharged_by_pipeline_validation': False}, {'category': 'compatibility_contract', 'kind': 'stored_format', 'description': 'Any move away from CBC, for example to GCM, changes the format of the encrypted DataStore file: a length byte, then the IV, then the ciphertext. Existing user settings files must stay readable. No migration path is shown.', 'discharged_by_pipeline_validation': False}, {'category': 'cause_unconfirmed', 'kind': 'key_provenance_unconfirmed', 'description': 'The source does not establish that the key at Cipher.init violates the generatedKey requirement. The createKey() branch uses KeyGenerator, and the other branch reads an AndroidKeyStore entry that the monitor does not track as a producer. No source change both satisfies the predicate and keeps the stored data readable.', 'discharged_by_pipeline_validation': False}], 'discharged_blockers': [], 'evidence_gap_promoted': ['cause_unconfirmed'], 'plan_publication_blockers': ['Analyzer reconfirmation: the pipeline cannot rerun the dynamic analyzer, so a reviewer must confirm that the monitor observes the KeyGenerator generation of the new key at the reported Cipher.init call (claim C3 is inferred only).', 'Stored format: reviewers must confirm that the marker byte keeps legacy files (first byte 16) readable and that the format change is acceptable for DataStore files.', 'Reviewer checklist: confirm that the reported call at CryptoManager.kt:42 is the intended one. Maintainers may separately review the CBC/no-authentication predicate as hardening.', 'Reviewer checklist: no test is planned because the repository has no test source set; run a manual read of a pre-patch settings file and a write/read round trip on a device.'], 'behavior_review': {'status': 'reviewed', 'review_contract_version': 23, 'regression_count': 0, 'patch_has_no_effect': False}}, 'digest_contract_assessment': {'security_relevance': 'false', 'contract_kind': 'unknown', 'expected_digest_source': '', 'backend_repository_available': False, 'backend_change_required': False, 'client_only_change_safe': False, 'rollout_strategy': '', 'pull_request_note': ''}, 'review_assumptions': ['Legacy files always start with IV length 16 (AES block size), so first byte 2 is unambiguous.', 'AndroidKeyStore KeyGenerator.getInstance(ALGORITHM) with a KeyGenParameterSpec selects the AndroidKeyStore provider at init, as the existing code already relies on.', 'Persisted file-format change is limited to a leading marker byte; legacy files remain readable and are rewritten in the new format on the next write.', 'Unknown first bytes other than 2 are treated as the legacy IV length, as before.', 'The plan entry for this file asks to update readFrom, but the CryptoManager contracts place all layout handling in decrypt, so the serializer already satisfies the plan with no edit.', 'Legacy settings files are assumed to be read by CryptoManager.decrypt exactly as before, and migration happens on the next DataStore write.', 'The marker byte 2 is assumed to be distinct from 16, the first byte of every legacy file.'], 'review_blockers': [], 'required_tests': [], 'decision': 'MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW', 'manual_review_required': True, 'auto_apply': False, 'publication_allowed': False, 'publication_status': 'blocked', 'semantic_validation': {'status': 'valid', 'errors': [], 'warnings': []}, 'stored_value_contract': {}, 'fix_scope': 'review_only', 'applied_for_validation': True, 'review_contract_version': 23, 'pr_attribution': {}, 'status': 'SUCCESS', 'error': None, 'original_method_body': '    private fun getKey(): SecretKey {\n        val existingKey = keyStore.getEntry("secret", null) as? KeyStore.SecretKeyEntry\n        return existingKey?.secretKey ?: createKey()\n    }\n\n    private fun createKey(): SecretKey {\n        return KeyGenerator.getInstance(ALGORITHM).apply {\n            init(\n                KeyGenParameterSpec.Builder(\n                    "secret",\n                    KeyProperties.PURPOSE_ENCRYPT or KeyProperties.PURPOSE_DECRYPT\n                )', 'corrected_method_body': '    private fun getKey(alias: String): SecretKey {\n        val existingKey = keyStore.getEntry(alias, null) as? KeyStore.SecretKeyEntry\n        return existingKey?.secretKey ?: createKey(alias)\n    }\n\n    private fun createKey(alias: String): SecretKey {\n        return KeyGenerator.getInstance(ALGORITHM).apply {\n            init(\n                KeyGenParameterSpec.Builder(\n                    alias,\n                    KeyProperties.PURPOSE_ENCRYPT or KeyProperties.PURPOSE_DECRYPT\n                )', 'finding_id': '013d2748f3f8', 'branch': 'fix/encrypt-cipherspec-013d2748f3f8-9298eb01fe', 'base_branch': 'master', 'base_commit': 'ca9adca05c5a73bd854e4dec52cf46415602514f', 'solution_revision': '9298eb01fe', 'worktree_attempt': 1, 'orphaned_worktree_paths': [], 'worktree_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/d_arm_sonnet_k3/pr_013d2748f3f8_r1/worktrees/com.yogeshpaliyal.keypass.debug_1442.apk/013d2748f3f8/9298eb01fe', 'base_repository_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/d_arm_sonnet_k3/pr_013d2748f3f8_r1/clones/com.yogeshpaliyal.keypass.debug_1442.apk', 'coordinated_edits': [{'source_file': 'common/src/main/java/com/yogeshpaliyal/common/utils/CryptoManager.kt', 'symbol': 'CryptoManager.getKey / createKey', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '    private fun getKey(): SecretKey {\n        val existingKey = keyStore.getEntry("secret", null) as? KeyStore.SecretKeyEntry\n        return existingKey?.secretKey ?: createKey()\n    }\n\n    private fun createKey(): SecretKey {\n        return KeyGenerator.getInstance(ALGORITHM).apply {\n            init(\n                KeyGenParameterSpec.Builder(\n                    "secret",\n                    KeyProperties.PURPOSE_ENCRYPT or KeyProperties.PURPOSE_DECRYPT\n                )', 'corrected_code': '    private fun getKey(alias: String): SecretKey {\n        val existingKey = keyStore.getEntry(alias, null) as? KeyStore.SecretKeyEntry\n        return existingKey?.secretKey ?: createKey(alias)\n    }\n\n    private fun createKey(alias: String): SecretKey {\n        return KeyGenerator.getInstance(ALGORITHM).apply {\n            init(\n                KeyGenParameterSpec.Builder(\n                    alias,\n                    KeyProperties.PURPOSE_ENCRYPT or KeyProperties.PURPOSE_DECRYPT\n                )', 'reason': 'Parameterize key alias so new data uses the app-generated "secret_v2" key while legacy data can still use "secret".'}, {'source_file': 'common/src/main/java/com/yogeshpaliyal/common/utils/CryptoManager.kt', 'symbol': 'CryptoManager.encrypt key', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, getKey())', 'corrected_code': '        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, getKey(KEY_ALIAS_V2))', 'reason': 'Encrypt with the new generated keystore key.'}, {'source_file': 'common/src/main/java/com/yogeshpaliyal/common/utils/CryptoManager.kt', 'symbol': 'CryptoManager.encrypt header', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '        outputStream.use {\n            it.write(iv.size)', 'corrected_code': '        outputStream.use {\n            it.write(FORMAT_VERSION_2)\n            it.write(iv.size)', 'reason': 'Write a version marker before the length byte so decrypt can distinguish new files from legacy ones.'}, {'source_file': 'common/src/main/java/com/yogeshpaliyal/common/utils/CryptoManager.kt', 'symbol': 'CryptoManager.decrypt', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '            val ivSize = inputStream.read()\n            val iv = ByteArray(ivSize)\n            inputStream.read(iv)\n\n            val cipher = Cipher.getInstance(TRANSFORMATION)\n            cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, getKey(), IvParameterSpec(iv))', 'corrected_code': '            val firstByte = inputStream.read()\n            val keyAlias: String\n            val ivSize: Int\n            if (firstByte == FORMAT_VERSION_2) {\n                keyAlias = KEY_ALIAS_V2\n                ivSize = inputStream.read()\n            } else {\n                // Legacy layout: the first byte is the IV length (16)\n                keyAlias = LEGACY_KEY_ALIAS\n                ivSize = firstByte\n            }\n            val iv = ByteArray(ivSize)\n            inputStream.read(iv)\n\n            val cipher = Cipher.getInstance(TRANSFORMATION)\n            cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, getKey(keyAlias), IvParameterSpec(iv))', 'reason': 'Select key and layout by the first byte: marker 2 uses the v2 key, otherwise legacy layout with the original key.'}, {'source_file': 'common/src/main/java/com/yogeshpaliyal/common/utils/CryptoManager.kt', 'symbol': 'CryptoManager.companion constants', 'edit_kind': 'constant', 'original_code': '        private const val TRANSFORMATION = "$ALGORITHM/$BLOCK_MODE/$PADDING"', 'corrected_code': '        private const val TRANSFORMATION = "$ALGORITHM/$BLOCK_MODE/$PADDING"\n        private const val LEGACY_KEY_ALIAS = "secret"\n        private const val KEY_ALIAS_V2 = "secret_v2"\n        private const val FORMAT_VERSION_2 = 2', 'reason': 'Add key aliases and the version marker (must differ from 16, the legacy first byte).'}], 'changed_files': ['common/src/main/java/com/yogeshpaliyal/common/utils/CryptoManager.kt'], 'quality_score': 70, 'explanation': '<!-- pr-title: Pass an alias to getKey so encrypt uses a generated secret_v2 key -->\nIn `CryptoManager.encrypt`, `Cipher.init` was given the key from `getKey()`, which looked up the keystore entry `secret` and fell back to `createKey()`. RVSec reported that, while the app ran, it observed no generator of the key passed to `Cipher.init`.\n\nI changed `getKey` and `createKey` to take a key alias. `encrypt` now calls `getKey(KEY_ALIAS_V2)`, so it uses a key made by `KeyGenerator` with `KeyGenParameterSpec` under the alias `secret_v2`. I made this change because RVSec reports the call, not because of a known problem in the app. Encrypted output now starts with a version byte (`2`) before the IV length. `decrypt` reads the first byte: `2` selects `secret_v2`, and any other value is taken as the IV length and uses the original `secret` alias.', 'applied_timestamp': '2026-11-16T05:18:28.211290+00:00'}], 'errors': []}

